  "limits": "Public/worker boundary cases execute the actual shell together with its dispatcher and canonical provider reader in an owned temporary package. Stubs return owned HTTP/GHA answers and log requests; Git ceiling prevents ancestor checkout leakage. BAD cases require exact codes/status/provider, exactly one selection, and no forbidden requests across approved rows a-e. Runtime unknown/2 is an unsafe-proceed refusal, not an unavailable control. GOOD success/recorded/advisory cases preserve intended behavior. The constructed bundle freezes the pre-change shell, flow module and provider reader together, with per-member hashes, so it cannot import a fixed current dispatcher and hide an old ref/mode defect. No live CI/network or independent provider identity authentication is claimed; existing provider-marker equality is preserved separately by tests.",
